From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Edwards <CFSworks@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 05 Jul 2026 17:35:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] net: dsa: rtl8365mb: hardware LAG offload with bridge uplink fixup

Add DSA port_lag_join/leave/change hooks and program the RTL8367-class
trunk tables so ge0+ge1 can hash in hardware when enslaved to bond0.

When bond0 sits on br0 (software bridge), ge0/ge1 leave DSA bridge
offload. Node->WAN traffic would hairpin through the 100M CPU port
(eth0) without explicit ASIC fixup. After HW trunk setup:

- extend port isolation so node ports and ge0/ge1 can reach each other
- set LAG member EFID to match br0 node ports (broadcast bridge domain)
- enable learning on LAG members for return traffic
- force LAG member STP state to FORWARDING (bonding driver may not
  propagate the bridge's STP state to DSA slaves; without this the ASIC
  blocks regular forwarding while DSA's offload_fwd_mark prevents the
  software bridge from compensating)
- re-enable unicast/multicast/broadcast flooding on LAG members (DSA
  clears the flooding masks when ports leave the bridge; without this
  the ASIC drops broadcast frames like ARP even though isolation allows
  the destination port)
- allow LAG members to forward to the CPU port (WAN -> br0/bond0 ingress)
- remap assisted-learning FDB adds on the CPU port to the first LAG
  member for remote hosts only (never remap the CPU netdev own MAC)
- re-run fixup when node ports join/leave br0 (bond comes up before
  bridge, so first fixup may see efid 0)

Also:
- set ds->num_lag_ids so DSA assigns lag->id (required for port_lag_join)
- allow single-member join in lag_can_offload: rejecting the first slave
  made DSA tear down LAG state so the second slave never saw two members
  (mv88e6xxx/qca allow single-member join; lag_refresh programs HW only
  when count reaches 2)
- limit trunk groups to 0-1 (only these have hash map registers)
- enable trunk dumb mode (CPU LACP + ASIC data plane; Realtek 802.1ad dumb)
- clear offload_fwd_mark in tag_rtl8_4 for broadcast/multicast from
  non-LAG ports when LAG is active (ARP/DHCP need software flood to bond0;
  unicast keeps the mark so ASIC trunk forwarding can run at wire speed
  once dumb-mode trunk is programmed)

Signed-off-by: Sam Edwards <CFSworks@gmail.com>
---
